Adaptor3d_HSurfaceTool: a B-spline surface is sampled by the knot spans
within the adaptor's range, not by all of the surface's (mitcad#235).

The intersections of a curve with a surface (IntCurveSurface, through the
edge-face intersections of the booleans) build a polyhedron of the
surface with NbSamplesU and NbSamplesV points, for a B-spline its number
of knots times its degree. A face on a part of a large surface was
sampled as the whole surface: a thread built as faces split every third
of a turn on surfaces that run all its 25 turns (about 4000 knots along
the helix) gave every piece's polyhedron 12000 rows, and the cut of the
thread spent 87 s of work (10 s on all cores) in the edge-face
intersections.

The counts are now the knot spans within the adaptor's range plus one,
times the degree (NbUIntervals and NbVIntervals at CN, which count the
spans between the range's knots): the same as before for an adaptor of the
whole surface, as dense as before within a part of it.

--- a/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Adaptor3d/Adaptor3d_HSurfaceTool.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKG3d/Adaptor3d/Adaptor3d_HSurfaceTool.cxx
@@ -33,7 +33,9 @@
     case GeomAbs_BezierSurface:
       return (3 + S->NbUPoles());
     case GeomAbs_BSplineSurface: {
-      const int nbs = S->NbUKnots() * S->UDegree();
+      // The knots within the adaptor's range (a face's), as many as the
+      // surface's own where the range is the whole surface.
+      const int nbs = (S->NbUIntervals(GeomAbs_CN) + 1) * S->UDegree();
       return (nbs < 2 ? 2 : nbs);
     }
     case GeomAbs_Torus:
@@ -53,7 +55,9 @@
     case GeomAbs_BezierSurface:
       return (3 + S->NbVPoles());
     case GeomAbs_BSplineSurface: {
-      const int nbs = S->NbVKnots() * S->VDegree();
+      // The knots within the adaptor's range (a face's), as many as the
+      // surface's own where the range is the whole surface.
+      const int nbs = (S->NbVIntervals(GeomAbs_CN) + 1) * S->VDegree();
       return (nbs < 2 ? 2 : nbs);
     }
     case GeomAbs_Cylinder:
